# @see R-030 (Design Patterns vs Native Platform Features)
id: PATTERN-009
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 4
action: advisory
title: Abstract Factory with only one concrete factory
category: quality
severity: info
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .tsx .js .java .kt .cs
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
patterns:
  - regex: abstract\s+class\s+\w*Factory
    message: "Abstract Factory — verify there are multiple concrete factories. A single implementation makes the abstraction premature (YAGNI)"
  - regex: interface\s+\w*Factory\s*\{
    message: "Factory interface — if only one class implements this, the interface adds indirection without polymorphism benefit"
  - regex: class\s+\w*FactoryImpl\s+(extends|implements)
    message: "FactoryImpl — the 'Impl' suffix with a single factory suggests over-engineering. Use a simple factory function or direct construction"
fix: If only one factory implementation exists, remove the abstract layer. Use a simple factory function or static create() method. Add abstraction when a second factory variant is actually needed.
